+Feature: Todo empty state
+  As a user visiting the TodoMVC app
+  I want to see a clean initial state
+  So that I understand how to begin adding todos
+
+  Rule: Empty app shows no todo list or footer
+
+    Scenario: Main section and footer are hidden when no todos exist
+      Given the app has no todos
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+    Scenario: New todo input is visible and focused on load
+      Given the app has no todos
+      Then the new todo input is visible
+      And the new todo input is focused
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence-and-routing.feature b/features/todo-persistence-and-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..438e796
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence-and-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence and routing
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads and to filter by status
+  So that I can track my tasks over time and focus on what matters
+
+  Rule: LocalStorage persistence
+
+    Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed state survives page reload
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Rule: Active items counter
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows number of active items
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      Then the todo list shows 1 item left
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses plural form for multiple items
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a todo "Buy eggs"
+      Then the todo list shows 2 items left
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses zero plural form
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list shows 0 items left
+
+  Rule: Route filtering
+
+    Scenario: All route shows all todos
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the "All" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+      And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs"
+      And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completing a todo hides it from the Active route
+      Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user clicks the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Uncompleting a todo hides it from the Completed route
+      Given the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user clicks the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
diff --git a/features/todo-toggle-all.feature b/features/todo-toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4a4e689
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+Feature: Toggle all todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete or active at once
+  So that I can batch-manage my task list
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checks all todos when activated
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks all todos when deactivated
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is not completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all reflects individual todo state
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all becomes checked when all todos are individually checked
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all becomes unchecked when a todo is unchecked
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app has a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+      When the user clicks the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
